<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:33:16Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>How China buried Tibet flood images after Nepal disaster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38aded01db10c4ad1cab2dfad25edfac79dd398b88db8055f68c3a8cfdb4dae3</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T14:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-china-buried-tibet-flood-images-after-nepal-disaster/a-78576472--f156a9510413.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-china-buried-tibet-flood-images-after-nepal-disaster/a-78576472?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In Tibet, a digital crackdown followed the deadly flood that has devastated communities along the China-Nepal border. Censors erased viral footage while Chinese state media flooded platforms with official content.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Deceived and deployed: How young Cameroonians end up fighting in Russia's war in Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d9ebf41301ac6978d4797f91290ebefb2a97abb76f718eca22ce63e310e2666</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/deceived-and-deployed-how-young-cameroonians-end-up-fighting-in-russia-s-war-in-ukraine/a-78513256--672bb0ec1fd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/deceived-and-deployed-how-young-cameroonians-end-up-fighting-in-russia-s-war-in-ukraine/a-78513256?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Analysts say economic desperation and fraudulent recruitment schemes are funneling Cameroonian youth into the Russian military — with deadly consequences.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tariffs spat: Carney bets Canada can defy Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a33f521e9a148e2fb2fd161b336279d4ad352eb884e4282cb535f50f0342bd3</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tariffs-spat-carney-bets-canada-can-defy-trump/a-78542754--cb80db02622b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tariffs-spat-carney-bets-canada-can-defy-trump/a-78542754?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canada is facing new US import penalties after Prime Minister Mark Carney refused to match US tariffs on China. Other countries are watching as the Trump trade clash turns into a fight over economic sovereignty.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Putin-Modi meeting at SCO: Can Russia-India ties hold?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88b053d17f3272f29e38e01558d77c0816e4e56500b3a6b8b59e8d18481a97e7</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:33:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/putin-modi-meeting-at-sco-can-russia-india-ties-hold/a-78575121--4d39471eea4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/putin-modi-meeting-at-sco-can-russia-india-ties-hold/a-78575121?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indian Prime Minister Modi and Russian President Putin are at the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) summit in Kyrgyzstan as Moscow and New Delhi face rising tensions with Washington.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal floods test PM Balen's young government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f8ef4478414c117d2dda67c21b44de0bbab784076f02cd7f0d3920989f33ff2</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:33:16Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T11:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-floods-test-pm-balen-s-young-government/a-78574227--fd76d80623d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-floods-test-pm-balen-s-young-government/a-78574227?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A year after Gen Z-led protests swept Prime Minister Balendra "Balen" Shah to power, deadly floods are testing his government's ability to manage a national crisis.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Niger's failed coup exposes cracks in the military — and Russia's influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08caca646547287fc910b073876a66c846d34af731ce2020c91a51592de73041</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T11:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/niger-s-failed-coup-exposes-cracks-in-the-military-and-russia-s-influence/a-78572278--256c8fdbe25e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/niger-s-failed-coup-exposes-cracks-in-the-military-and-russia-s-influence/a-78572278?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The failed coup in Niger has brought deep divisions within the military to light. As Russia's support highlights the junta's fading influence, soldiers continue to face jihadi attacks, poor equipment and little pay.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Guinea-Bissau votes to reshape presidency</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d38ee92fc62bb770e65a5df49abc398148f2b5de7f2bf00fc7ebae43bf47d93</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T12:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-votes-to-reshape-presidency/a-78562523--6d1dcf4a63cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-votes-to-reshape-presidency/a-78562523?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The West African nation's military government wants to amend the constitution to give more powers to the president. The junta, which seized power last year, says it will hold elections in December.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Greece, Turkey clash over protected Aegean marine areas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5068e4eb9fc4ab602e54bf1e8badd02564b9e674fa2ffd5801e1d08b42592312</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/greece-turkey-clash-over-protected-aegean-marine-areas/a-78550021--198e60df237d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/greece-turkey-clash-over-protected-aegean-marine-areas/a-78550021?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkey has announced the creation of two protected zones in a disputed area of the Aegean Sea, sparking an angry reaction from Greece. Does this mark a new chapter in a long-running dispute between the two countries?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's citizen-led school audits test limits of activism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19ef3e27df9480299eafaf3249d2833a2fc6a77b54eb80b799b274d3e805f88f</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-citizen-led-school-audits-test-limits-of-activism/a-78545789--41cb1b89184e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-citizen-led-school-audits-test-limits-of-activism/a-78545789?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The student-led "Cockroach" movement is taking its campaign for accountability to government schools, but the activists' methods are encountering growing resistance from authorities.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal issues fresh flood warning as 3,000 still missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe489dd44d861d8fbb73f9c5502b361e2a5db0517c3f1e0d9589884ed5882c16</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T06:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-issues-fresh-flood-warning-as-3-000-still-missing/a-78561068--69ee48f29b5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-issues-fresh-flood-warning-as-3-000-still-missing/a-78561068?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rescuers are trying to reach dozens of hydropower workers trapped in flooded tunnels, but have been hampered by further rainfall.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli settlers attack Palestinian homes in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e434467efd5bef87315e57c6c889911b94290b4806872d5011e6d10ed3e57751</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T19:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israeli-settlers-attack-palestinian-homes-in-west-bank/a-78560116--bdbba5c25b66.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-settlers-attack-palestinian-homes-in-west-bank/a-78560116?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Masked Israeli settlers launched their first major attack since initiating a siege in the village of Qusra earlier this month. Saturday's attacks were met with rare criticism from Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
